   800	   * cost of repeated history reads to O(limit) instead of a full synchronous
   801	   * re-read of the (up to 75k-line) message log per call. Holds the most recent
   802	   * TAIL_CACHE_LIMIT entries per topic, which covers every production caller
   803	   * (live-tail + handoff hash use 500, respawn history far less). Log rotation
   804	   * is irrelevant to it — rotation only drops OLD lines, and the cache only
   805	   * holds the newest.
