docs/specs/reaper-toctou-fix.eli16.md:4:Your agent creates temporary copies of the codebase (called "worktrees") when it builds things. A background cleaner ("the reaper") removes the ones that are finished — safely, only when a worktree's branch is already merged, has no unsaved changes, and nothing is using it.
