docs/specs/calm-transient-episode-alerting.md:35:- On heal, `closeEpisode` unconditionally emits a `resolve` effect → a second, NOTIFYING hub message; nothing bounds resolve volume for a cycling condition. The reopen path's `raise` with a reused id is silently swallowed (the operator is never told a divergence returned).
docs/specs/calm-transient-episode-alerting.md:64:- **Persistence discipline:** anchors are new fields in the episode manager's EXISTING durable per-machine file (`version: 1` unchanged; strictly additive — the reader is lenient to unknown fields, and a binary rollback treats them as inert). Writes remain transitions-only: anchor fields persist on MATERIAL change (onset set/clear, an observed version change, a flap event, a derived-raise latch, or an `activeSkewMs` bucket boundary of ≥5 min) — a tick observing no change writes nothing.
docs/specs/calm-transient-episode-alerting.md:77:- **Expectation honesty:** a single-hop laggard (old → latest in one restart — the auto-updater's normal shape) never "advances" mid-wave; its first advance IS the heal. M-P1 helps multi-version crawls and slow waves; the 2026-07-11 incident shape still confirms at 45 min — its operator-visible improvement comes from M-P2's silent calm class. Live-pair verification is read against this calibration.
docs/specs/calm-transient-episode-alerting.md:95:- **Delivery-true demotion predicate:** an informational escalation is demoted to the audit log + digest ONLY when, on the raising machine, ALL hold LIVE at demotion time: `monitoring.ropeHealth` enabled, `digestTopicId` set, AND the digest job is actually runnable IN THIS PROCESS — defined as a live LOCAL handle check: a `JobScheduler` instance is running in this process AND the `rope-health-digest` job is loaded and enabled (the lease read is at most a fast-path pre-check, never the conjunct: the scheduler is constructed only at boot when awake, so a standby PROMOTED to lease-holder at runtime holds the lease with NO scheduler until restart — the lease proxy would pass exactly where nothing delivers). Any miss ⇒ fall back to today's hub attention item. Config presence is NOT delivery capability; the non-lease-holder and the promoted-standby both take the fallback arm (the promoted-standby case joins wiring test #4).
docs/specs/calm-transient-episode-alerting.md:117:- remediation-actions: the auto-updater (existing, independent; this guard invokes nothing — it OBSERVES heal progress via advert version advances)
docs/specs/calm-transient-episode-alerting.md:169:- **Integration:** simulated wave (skew → advance → extend → heal → ZERO notifying messages; silent raise + silent bounded resolve visible in the hub); stall path (no advance → silent calm raise → ceiling → notifying `:stalled` HIGH with prompt → heal → all items DONE + ONE notifying close note); flap path (3 genuine cycles → `:recurring` once, cap-exempt, once per 24 h across episode churn); wave-backstop path (6 calm onsets across keys → one notifying aggregate); nickname-escaping regression on the new message shapes (pins PR #1454).
