docs/specs/CARTOGRAPHER-SWEEP-EVENTLOOP-SAFETY.md:88:**Every failure path sets `refused: true` (Adversarial Finding 9).** `detect-timeout`, `detect-worker-start-failure`, `detect-index-too-large`, `detect-git-error` must ALL set `refused: true` + a `refusalReason`, so they flow through `classifyProgress`'s `r.refused` branch and feed the breaker — otherwise a result with `candidateCount: 0, refused: false` is mistaken for "genuinely nothing to do," resets the breaker accounting, and the sweep silently does nothing forever. Unit test asserts each refusal increments `zeroProgressTicks`, not `consecutiveZeroCandidate`.
docs/specs/CARTOGRAPHER-SWEEP-EVENTLOOP-SAFETY.md:90:**Worker env is an allowlist, not the full process env (Security Finding 1).** The worker is spawned with an explicit minimal `env` (`PATH`, `HOME`, the `GIT_*` it needs) — never the parent `process.env`, which holds the Telegram token, Anthropic keys, Bearer authToken, and dashboard PIN material that the detect worker has no need for. This matches the existing Codex-spawn env-allowlist discipline. Unit test asserts a sentinel secret var is absent in the spawned worker's visible env.
docs/specs/CARTOGRAPHER-SWEEP-EVENTLOOP-SAFETY.md:106:- **`GET /cartographer/health`** serves the **entire** freshness block (both `health()` *and* the former `freshnessHealth()` fields) from the snapshot — closing starver 4. Backward-compat is **additive**: the existing field names/semantics (`nodeCount`, `staleCount`, `authoredCount`, `freshness.*`) are preserved, sourced from the snapshot (Integration Finding 3). New fields: `snapshot: 'present'|'absent'|'detect-failing'`, `generatedAt`, `headSha`, plus a server-computed **`snapshotStale: boolean`** + `ageMs` + `headMoved: boolean` (computed from one cheap `git rev-parse --short HEAD` — never a walk) so consumers don't have to interpret a timestamp (Adversarial Finding 3, Lessons Finding 6). `lastDetectStatus` (`ok|timeout|worker-start-failed|index-too-large|git-error`) + `lastDetectAt` surface detect health so a broken detect is visible on the route, distinct from `snapshot:'absent'` = never-run (Adversarial Finding 1, Integration Finding 8).
