docs/specs/telegram-egress-invisible-payload-guard.eli16.md:66:character pair, and accent marks with no letter to sit on. **All of those passed as "visible" and would have
docs/specs/telegram-egress-invisible-payload-guard.eli16.md:67:been sent.** Every one shows a reader nothing — the same harm as the original incident, hiding inside the fix
docs/specs/telegram-egress-invisible-payload-guard.eli16.md:77:than hidden: some future character could be officially a letter and still look like nothing, and that would
docs/specs/telegram-egress-invisible-payload-guard.eli16.md:98:itself, because an invisible message is still someone's content.
docs/specs/telegram-egress-invisible-payload-guard.eli16.md:102:Almost certainly nothing, and that's the intent. Real messages send exactly as before — including a message
docs/specs/telegram-egress-invisible-payload-guard.eli16.md:103:that's just a full stop, which is visible and therefore fine.
