docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:5:UNSOUND — three independent egress/model mismatches can admit content that Telegram renders as nothing. Three additional load-bearing claims are false of the code or Telegram’s live grammar. Previously stated-open defects are not counted again.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:15:   [invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:125) classifies `sendRichMessage` and `sendRichMessageDraft` as accepting alternative fields `text` and `rich_message`. They do not: the live API requires only `rich_message` for both methods ([sendRichMessage](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#sendrichmessage), [sendRichMessageDraft](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#sendrichmessagedraft)), and the server reads only `rich_message` ([official implementation](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api/blob/master/telegram-bot-api/Client.cpp#L11607-L11619)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:19:   Concrete failure path: a rich-message request supplies a harmless visible query `text` and carries the actual reader-invisible `rich_message` in a byte-oriented JSON body. The door treats unsupported `text` as decisive, never inspects the body, and sends it; Telegram ignores `text` and consumes `rich_message`.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:21:   The pinning test repeats the wrong table while claiming live-documentation verification ([telegram-send-funnel-invisible-payload.test.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/tests/unit/telegram-send-funnel-invisible-payload.test.ts:542)), disproving the spec’s assertion that this pin makes silent drift impossible ([spec](/Users/justin/window12-exam/docs/specs/telegram-egress-invisible-payload-guard.md:329)). This is an intersection of declared residuals, not a recount of either one alone.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:25:   `structuredTextLeaves` loops through every property and recursively descends every object-valued property ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:432)). Telegram instead selects a `type` discriminator and extracts only that variant’s defined fields before returning; for example, URL consumes `text` and `url`, while reference consumes `text` and `name` ([official parser](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api/blob/master/telegram-bot-api/Client.cpp#L11326-L11443)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:27:   Concrete failure path: a valid wrapper has an invisible real label and an extra, server-ignored nested member containing a visible-looking `text` leaf. The door counts the ignored leaf and allows; Telegram discards it and renders only the invisible label.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:29:   This contradicts the source claim that the walker visits “exactly” the literals ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:368)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:35:   The walker classifies `expression` as an ordinary unformatted string ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:432)), then accepts it whenever source characters satisfy the Unicode predicate ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:464)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:37:   Concrete failure path: a valid layout/spacing-only LaTeX expression contains letters or punctuation in its source but paints no visible glyph. The source passes while the rendered message is empty. This extends CMT-1260 beyond its stated HTML/Markdown scope.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:39:4. **PRECISION — the test advertised as exercising the “REAL RichText grammar” uses invalid Bot API discriminator values.**
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:41:   [telegram-egress-boundary.test.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/tests/unit/telegram-egress-boundary.test.ts:332) uses `richTexts`, `richTextBold`, `richTextPlain`, and block type `math`. The Bot API uses a bare array for a sequence and discriminator values such as `bold` and `mathematical_expression`; unsupported types are rejected by Telegram’s parser ([official parser](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api/blob/master/telegram-bot-api/Client.cpp#L11312-L11447)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:47:   [invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:401) says `name` is the displayed reference label and that excluding it wrongly refuses a reference whose only visible content is its name.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:51:   The comment’s concrete failure path does not exist: a visible reference label is already walked through `text`. Applying the suggested discriminator repair to count `name` would instead count a non-rendered identifier and could introduce an under-refusal.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:55:   [window12-closeout.md](/Users/justin/window12-exam/docs/specs/reports/window12-closeout.md:40) says the closed world contains 17 methods: four reader-visible plus 13 bodyless.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:57:   The code contains six reader-visible methods ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:125)) and 13 bodyless methods ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:184)), totaling 19. The same closeout later reports 19 ([window12-closeout.md](/Users/justin/window12-exam/docs/specs/reports/window12-closeout.md:207)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:69:- **`answerCallbackQuery`:** Still a stated product judgment rather than a mechanical no-content fact; it remains bodyless ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:176)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:71:- **`editForumTopic`:** Still guarded unconditionally through `name`; empty-name/preserve-current semantics remain unmodeled ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:140)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:73:- **Local Bot API Server:** Still outside runtime and lint recognition because both hard-code `api.telegram.org` ([telegram-egress.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:60), [lint](/Users/justin/window12-exam/scripts/lint-telegram-egress-boundary.mjs:48)). Telegram supports replacing the cloud endpoint with a [local server](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api#moving-a-bot-to-a-local-server).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:81:- **Structured content only in JSON bodies:** Still open. Query/form/multipart collection leaves `rich_message` as a JSON-serialized string, after which JSON punctuation satisfies the scalar predicate.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:83:- **Cross-field query/body precedence:** Still open and unsafe. The waiver uses `fields.some(...)` ([telegram-egress.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:389)), but Telegram’s `editMessageText` chooses `rich_message` whenever present before falling back to `text` ([official implementation](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api/blob/master/telegram-bot-api/Client.cpp#L13605-L13612)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:85:- **Destination fields:** Excluding live URL/e-mail/phone/anchor/reference-link destinations remains correct because the displayed label is `text`. The claimed `RichTextReference.name` exception is wrong, per Finding 5. `document`/`RichTextIcon` is absent from the live Bot API RichText union, so the “live grammar” comment is also stale there.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:87:- **No-leaf structures:** Still open and unsafe. All no-leaf objects are allowed ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:464)), but the union contains both visible media/dividers and non-rendered anchors. Telegram expressly permits an empty named anchor.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:89:- **Normalized host spellings in lint:** Still open. The prefilter and recognizer depend on literal `api.telegram.org/` source text rather than URL semantics ([lint](/Users/justin/window12-exam/scripts/lint-telegram-egress-boundary.mjs:51)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:91:- **`fetch.call`/`fetch.apply`:** Still open. The callee is recognized, but analysis always treats argument zero as the URL ([lint](/Users/justin/window12-exam/scripts/lint-telegram-egress-boundary.mjs:151)); for `call` it is the receiver, while `apply` stores arguments in an array. No canary covers either.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:95:- **Rendering shortcut / CMT-1260:** Still open. HTML/Markdown are locally approximated ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:298)); the stated malformed-tag over-refusal and encoded/delimiter under-refusals remain. Its description is incomplete because LaTeX adds Finding 3.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:97:- **Surviving per-sender guard:** Still open exactly as described. The tokenless standby checks before sending text to another machine ([TelegramAdapter.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/TelegramAdapter.ts:1380)); this process’s door cannot observe the eventual Bot API request.
