docs/specs/codex-full-parity-fixes.eli16.md:15:When a turn ends, three checkers are supposed to run: a tone/coherence check, an anti-confabulation check, and a scope-drift check. On Codex we accidentally swapped one of them out for a checker that belongs at a totally different moment — and that misplaced one just sits there doing nothing. Fix: put the right three back, and move the misplaced one to where it actually belongs.
docs/specs/codex-full-parity-fixes.eli16.md:19:The anti-deferral checker reads the data in Claude's format. Codex hands it the same information with different labels, so the checker shrugs and does nothing. (I proved this directly — fed it both formats and watched it work for Claude, ignore Codex.) Fix: teach it to read both, exactly like we already did for the dangerous-command guard.
