docs/specs/MESH-SELF-HEAL-G3-BUILD.md:36:- 2026-06-27 18:4x PDT: 📋 **Live-verify scenario matrix drafted** → `docs/specs/MESH-SELF-HEAL-G3-LIVE-VERIFY.md` (the test-as-self FINAL gate per Justin's explicit directive + the Live-User-Channel-Proof standard). 8 scenarios (happy-path / lifecycle-binding-IFF / the core duplicate bug / channel-parity / idempotency / concurrency / rollback / regression), each with PASS criterion + evidence; throwaway TEST topic for destructive bits; flip flag ON for the pair to verify ENFORCEMENT; honesty rules (Laptop-dark ⇒ two-machine scenarios BLOCKED, never simulated). Execute AFTER commit. Full-suite re-run in flight (commit gate) — first run 5 fails/32358 (the 1 visible = load-induced supertest ETIMEDOUT in unrelated sharedStateRoutesV2; re-running lighter to confirm flake-vs-real before commit).
docs/specs/MESH-SELF-HEAL-G3-BUILD.md:43:  - ✅ **immediate-clear-on-kill is spec-correct** (NOT a drain-then-clear violation): a KILLed session is already gone — nothing to drain through a corpse; the durable inbound queue carries any in-flight message to the new owner keyed by topic. The bounded drain-then-clear / wedge-short-circuit / claim-reclaim (§3.3 round-2/3 Adv) are TRANSFER-path concerns owned by the closeout/drain machinery, not the kill-listener.
