docs/specs/SELF-PROPAGATION-HARNESS-SPEC.eli16.md:15:**Part 1 — make the "two listeners" problem impossible (you picked this).** Instead of relying on a flag, the lifeline leaves a little "I've got the listening covered" note. The server checks for that note on startup; if it's there and current, the server automatically stays quiet. Now it doesn't matter how the server was started — it can't double-listen. (If there's no note, the server behaves exactly as today, so nothing else changes.)
