docs/specs/ROBUST-SESSION-TIME-AWARENESS-SPEC.md:37:1. **No time-box record ⇒ no tracking (the actual incident).** A time-boxed mandate run in **`/loop` dynamic mode** (self-paced `ScheduleWakeup`) writes **no durable started/duration record**. With no record, nothing can compute elapsed/remaining, and the autonomous-stop-hook — the one component that *does* track time — is inert (it keys on `.instar/autonomous-state.local.md`, which `/loop` never creates). The agent flew blind and rationalised a stop. **`/loop` is a Claude Code harness skill instar cannot modify** — so the fix is NOT to instrument `/loop`, it is to make the agent **create an autonomous-state record for any time-boxed run** and to make tracking read that record.
