docs/specs/autonomous-progress-heartbeat.eli16.md:7:When the agent is running a long autonomous job, it sometimes goes heads-down for a long stretch — building, fixing tests, running sub-agents — doing real work the whole time, but never sending the operator a message. From the operator's chair, an hour of silence looks exactly like the agent froze or died. That actually happened on 2026-06-16: the agent worked for about an hour straight fixing a pull request, said nothing, and the operator had to ask "did you stall?"
docs/specs/autonomous-progress-heartbeat.eli16.md:13:Our first idea was a simple timer that every so often posted "Still working — N minutes since my last update." We threw that out. Instar already did a big piece of approved work (HONEST-PROGRESS-MESSAGING) that DELETED exactly that kind of "still on it, nothing new" filler, because a periodic "still working" line carries no real information and just trains the operator to ignore the channel. Re-adding it under a new name would undo that honesty work.
