docs/specs/codex-full-parity-fixes.md:25:The enforcement-hook-layer spec wired instar's gates onto Codex. Driving codey live (test-as-self, 2026-05-25) proved that **wiring ≠ working**: several gates are registered but inert, the end-of-turn review trio is structurally wrong, the dashboard mislabels Codex sessions, and — the headline — Codex's hook **trust model** means a freshly-initialized Codex agent has **all gates dead** until a human clicks a trust prompt, which an autonomous agent cannot do. This is the exact "looks installed, does nothing" trap (`Structure > Willpower` failure at the enforcement layer).
