docs/specs/prompt-gate-no-prompt-cache.md:23:The historical evolution explains the bug: the rate limiter was originally named for its actual semantic — *throttle relays to the user* — and was correctly set only on emit. Later, the gate at the start of `llmDetect` was repurposed to also gate LLM calls (not just relays), but the set-site wasn't updated. The naming/semantics drift went unnoticed because the symptom (excessive cost) was diffuse and only became visible once the token ledger was running.
