docs/specs/reports/remote-session-close-convergence.md:16:- **Honesty rules for a destructive action at a distance:** a timeout now reports "outcome unknown — refreshing" (the close may have landed; claiming "nothing happened" would be a fake failure); a second click on an already-closing session reads "already closed," not a scary error; non-JSON tunnel errors are normalized so the real reason reaches your screen; and the relayed origin note in the owner's log is recorded as an unverified claim, never trusted for any decision.
