docs/specs/reports/skill-concept-convergence.md:17:A few things were honestly deferred. The biggest is the backfill migration: existing agents' canonical directory is empty (they store skills directly under `.claude/skills/`), so the parity rule has nothing to verify on them. The fix is a `PostUpdateMigrator` entry that backfills canonical from existing renderings on first run; this is tracked as a follow-up PR and the spec is explicit that the prototype is no-op-on-existing-agents until it lands. Similarly, `allowed-tools` rendering was removed from the v0.1 frontmatter rather than promising tool-restriction the renderer doesn't enforce — that surface lands with the Tool primitive.
