docs/specs/promise-beacon-escalation.eli16.md:25:Mostly invisible when things work — promises just quietly get kept even if a session dies in the middle. When they *can't* be kept, you get an honest heads-up instead of silence. It ships turned off, then in a watch-only "here's what I would have done" mode first, and only goes live after that evidence looks clean — so it can't misbehave on the way in.
