docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:40:| **NEW standard: Judgment Within Floors** (§7 — *derives from* Signal vs. Authority + The Body and the Mind; sharpens, does not invert) | Gap (stated precisely): the registry tells a builder that invariants are structural and the mind holds final authority above the floor — nothing tells a builder HOW to place the boundary at a competing-signals decision point, or what a delegation must carry (floor, default, ladder, provenance). |
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:42:| **NEW standard: Ownership-Gated Side Effects** | Gap: nothing requires session-creating/reviving actors to prove conversation ownership at fire time (revival actors do it ad-hoc — §2.4; the interactive spawn path doesn't). |
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:74:The post-transfer closeout — immediate half at `src/commands/server.ts:21982-22006`, reaper-tick sweeper via `SessionReaper` (`src/monitoring/SessionReaper.ts:1009-1024`, terminate at `:893-958`, config `topicMovedCloseout:true`, `topicMovedConfirmTicks:2`, `topicMovedVetoBreakerAttempts:5` at `:153-155`, F8 lease carve-out `bypassLeaseForTopicMovedCloseout` at `:919-928`) — is gated on `topicOwnerElsewhere` = `reg.ownerOf(topicId) !== self` (`src/commands/server.ts:8972-8979`). A deliberate move WRITES that ownership record; an independently-spawned duplicate does not. On the Mini the registry had NO active record for these topics (hence `owner=?` in the route log), so `ownerOf` gave nothing to compare and the sweeper never fired. **The missing piece is not a new closer — it is a converged ownership record.** Note also the two-source-of-truth wrinkle: the Mini's PIN store knew the Laptop held 29836 (`hard-pin-unsatisfiable`) while its ownership registry held no record; §3.2 reconciles both.
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:82:The authority skip ladder (`SessionManager.terminateSession`, `src/core/SessionManager.ts:1311-1430`): protected → not-lease-holder (`:1344-1348`) → ReapGuard cascade (`src/core/ReapGuard.ts:131-224`: spawn-grace, recovery-in-flight, pending-injection, relay-lease, recent-user-message, open-commitment, active-subagent, structural-long-work, active-process; guard-error → KEEP) → in-flight. The Laptop's copies were shielded by `not-lease-holder`, the Mini's by `open-commitment`. Each guard is individually correct; jointly they make a duplicate immortal. **Round-1 correction (verified):** the F8 carve-out precedent lifts ONLY the lease gate — `attemptCloseoutTerminate` re-checks every other KEEP guard fresh (`SessionManager.ts:1284-1294`), and `open-commitment` is topic-scoped and re-armed by owner-side user traffic (`ReapGuard.ts:66-79,183-193`). A converged record alone therefore does NOT dissolve the Mini-side shield; §3.2.4a addresses it explicitly. **Round-2 correction (verified):** the `open-commitment` guard keys on `activeCommitmentForTopic(topicId)` — TOPIC-scoped; the `Commitment` record carries `topicId`/`boundTuple`/`boundBy` and NO session-binding field (`src/monitoring/CommitmentTracker.ts:35-75`), so there is nothing session-shaped to "re-bind"; custody semantics are record-level and cross-machine (§3.2.4a).
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:119:Rollout flag: `multiMachine.sessionPool.ownershipGatedSpawn` (shape + semantics in §4). **Enforcement precondition (round-2, codex):** Layer A ENFORCES only on a pool whose inbound queue is live (rung-3 durable custody exists there); everywhere else it runs dryRun. The §3.3 matrix's "fleet today" row describes the DRYRUN would-be path, not an enforceable state — refusing to spawn with nothing but a resend notice would trade reachability for coherence, and the honest trade (§3.7) only clears once custody exists.
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:124:Layer B's enforcement flip is **gated on the durable + replicated ownership substrate being live on every pool machine** (`LocalSessionOwnershipStore` + journal materialization, pool-consistent activation — the existing `server.ts:18952-18963` signal pattern). On the fleet default (in-memory store, no replication) `other-alive`/`other-dark` are unresolvable cross-machine and convergence writes are meaningless; the reconciler refuses to arm there (a loud `substrate-not-ready` status, never silent). **Substrate flap:** readiness is re-evaluated per tick; a NOT-ready tick pauses the reconciler (status + one deduped item if it persists >30 min), while the seam keeps running on its local cached view — replication degradation degrades seam verdicts toward the `unowned`/`error` arms, both bounded-loud. All three pool-behavior flags — `ownershipGatedSpawn`, `duplicateReconciler`, AND `commitmentCustodyTransfer` — join the machine-coherence guard's coherence-critical set (`COHERENCE_CRITICAL_FLAGS`, `src/core/machineCoherenceManifest.ts:93`; custody skew degrades escalate-safe, but a split pool should still be visible) — noting honestly that the guard itself is dev-gated dryRun-first, so **pool-consistent activation is the PRIMARY defense** against flag skew; the guard is the alarm layer where it runs.
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:153:- **Post-close commitment custody transfer (record-level, origin-stamp-preserving; its own sub-feature, round-3):** after a `duplicate-reconciled` (or `topic-moved`, below) close SUCCEEDS, the reconciler drives custody: it reads the closed copy's machine's open topic-scoped commitments (existing authenticated mesh read), the OWNER machine mints successor commitments through its own existing `POST /commitments` API with idempotent `externalKey` = `custody:<topicId>:<origin-commitment-id>` (the successor carries the origin's `userRequest`/`agentResponse`/`type`/`topicId` and a `custodyOf` cross-ref; peer-derived free text is **type/length-clamped and envelope-treated on receive** like every replicated-store ingest; the mint respects the owner's `maxActiveBeacons` activation cap), and on ACK the ORIGIN machine mutates its own records (its own single-writer CAS, via a dedicated origin-side supersede verb — §8) to a terminal `superseded-by-ownership-move` state — audited, beacon-terminal, never counted as violated (`sessionEpoch`'s `session-lost` check is disarmed by the terminal state; `supersededBy` precedent, `CommitmentTracker.ts:121`). **The supersede is fenced to a VERIFIED successor:** it requires the successor's externalKey + owner machineId and verifies successor existence via the authenticated mesh read before the CAS — no bare Bearer caller can terminal-supersede a live commitment. No ACK → the origin records stay untouched and ONE `custody-transfer-failed` item escalates (the promise is never silently dropped; `PromiseBeacon`'s existing owner-other self-suppression covers the gap window without duplicate beaconing). A VETOED close transfers nothing — custody moves only after a confirmed close, so there is no rollback path to get wrong. **Rollout boundary:** custody transfer ships behind its own sub-flag `multiMachine.sessionPool.commitmentCustodyTransfer` (independently reversible, Increment 2b, its own two-node E2E); with it disabled or unavailable, an open-commitment duplicate is NOT auto-closed — it escalates (`custody-transfer-unavailable`), the safe degradation.
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:157:A topic re-duplicating ≥3 times in 24h stops being auto-reconciled and raises ONE attention item. Counters are **per-topic episode counts in the replicated store**, receive-side type-clamped like every replicated store (finite bounded numbers, ISO-8601 timestamps; reject otherwise — an unclamped peer row must not clamp a conversation's ladder), TTL-pruned when idle >24h; counter rows ride the replication journal's post-fix size bounding (the 50MB-bloat fix — declared, not assumed). Record FLIPS and echoed-but-unhealed episodes count toward the breaker; transfer-traceable episodes do not clamp — but ≥3 transfer-traceable episodes per topic per 24h raise ONE observability-only attention item (round-3: a flapping automated mover must not be invisible just because it is exempt from the clamp; the transfer path's own 409 rate limit is the brake). **Breaker-open also clamps the owner-dark ladder for that topic to rung 3** (no claim-then-spawn), so the duplicate GENERATOR is braked together with the healer.
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:178:3. **Queue + honest notice** — death unprovable (wobbly-but-alive): durable-queue custody when the inbound queue is live; when it is dark, the deterministic floor is **notice-only, with state-accurate wording** (FD9): dark-queue *"That conversation's machine is temporarily unreachable (it may be restarting). I can't safely answer from here, and I'm not holding your message — please resend in a few minutes, or send it to my Lifeline topic if it's urgent."*; queue-live *"…your message is saved and will be answered automatically when it returns."* Delivered on the **deterministic G1 path** (`telegram.sendToTopic` — the cold-start-lifeline precedent), **bypassing speaker election with a declared owner-dark exception** (election rule 1 is owner-liveness-blind, §2.6, and would structurally silence the notice). Guards on the exception: a **final owner-liveness re-check immediately before the send** (shrinks the contradictory-voices window to the probe RTT — a just-recovered owner answering normally suppresses the notice), plus a **topic-scoped suppression check** (recent identical notice visible in the topic's send history — episode dedupe is machine-scoped, so under split-brain two front doors could otherwise each notice; round-2). Dedupe: ONE notice per (topic, outage-episode), per-topic cooldown 30 min (`noticeCooldownMs`). Owner recovery closes the episode.
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:225:- **The honest user-visible trade (round-2, adversarial):** today a wobbly-owner message gets an INSTANT answer from a fresh wrong-machine session — which splits the conversation's context across machines and mints an immortal duplicate (the incident). Under enforcement it gets custody-or-notice. One resend beats a context-less answer plus a duplicate; this is stated here so the fleet flip survives the operator's inevitable "why did my agent stop answering instantly?" — and it is exactly why enforcement WAITS for durable-queue custody (§3.1) rather than shipping notice-only.
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:259:- **Unit:** tri-state resolver (each kind incl. thrown-registry → `error`, windowed breaker incl. interleaved-success flapping, hysteresis close, episode counting); admission table exhaustive incl. router-verdict consumption; ladder rung transitions + FULL stage matrix (queue × hold × release) + silence ceiling + notice dedupe + pre-send liveness re-check; intended-owner rules (admissible-epoch beats recency; origin-stamp rejection; both-self; rule-2/rule-3 contradiction → escalate; both-run → escalate; quarantined pin ignored; 409 → escalate; boot-time epoch re-seed); arbiter clamps (invalid/omitted/timeout/below-floor → default, action-space violation rejected, defer cap → escalate at 4, move without PRE-EPISODE corroboration rejected — incl. a post-episode-minted commitment); custody transfer (idempotent externalKey re-mint, ACK-gated supersede fenced to verified successor, no-ACK escalate, vetoed-close transfers nothing, sessionEpoch disarm, beacon-cap respected, custody-disabled → escalate); carve-out (disposition-appropriate fence required on BOTH legs — reason-string forgery rejected for `duplicate-reconciled` AND `topic-moved`; terminate-time probe fail → veto); episode-open backdating (post-spawn evidence rejected even when detection lags); provenance writer (schema, scrub, {redacted,full} split, byte clamps, async buffering, sampling); breaker (replicated counters survive lease move, type-clamped receive rejects NaN/2^53, flip + echoed-but-unhealed counting, transfer-traceable exclusion, TTL prune).
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:299:14. **Custody-transfer mechanics** (§3.2.4a): post-close only; owner-side mint = existing `POST /commitments` + externalKey `custody:<topicId>:<origin-commitment-id>` + `custodyOf` cross-ref (origin fields carried: userRequest/agentResponse/type/topicId, clamped+enveloped on receive); origin-side supersede verb fenced to the verified successor; 5s per-step timeout; failure → `custody-transfer-failed` escalation; vetoed close transfers nothing; own sub-flag (Increment 2b) with escalate-not-close degradation.
docs/specs/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors.md:330:**Traces to the goal.** Observable Intelligence — no autonomous decision is invisible, and the system's judgment measurably improves.
