docs/specs/MESH-SELF-HEAL-SPEC.md:94:**Resolution is SINGLE-CLAIMANT through the fenced lease (findings Adv-F2, Adv-F6, Les-A1; round-2 Adv2-F1, Int2-B).** The claim is NOT each machine independently deciding "am I fit?" — that is the split-brain double-poll bug. Exactly one machine claims, chosen deterministically: **the F4-preferred-awake machine if it is itself fit, else the lowest-machineId fit machine** (finding DC-OQ2). The claimant acquires poll-ownership by **winning the fenced epoch-CAS** (the same authority that gates the lease). **CAS-win is necessary but NOT sufficient (round-2 Adv2-F1):** because fitness was assessed from heartbeat-cadence-LAGGING advertised booleans, after winning the CAS the claimant MUST RE-VERIFY its OWN live `pollSucceededMonoMs` freshness (current, local) before committing to serve; on self-unfit it immediately relinquishes the epoch (signed tombstone + the G1 quiesce) AND immediately advertises `pollFresh:false` + a `selfExcludedThisEpisode` flag in its signed heartbeat (round-3 Adv3-F-A: re-electing "excluding itself" is locally-scoped and invisible to peers — without this, peers re-run their election over the lagged advertised set and re-nominate the just-relinquished machine until cadence propagates `pollFresh:false`, leaving a fit peer unselected for ~one heartbeat interval). The immediate self-demotion advertisement makes peers' next election skip it at once. Bounded by `confirmObservations` so it cannot ping-pong. **Actuation seam (round-2 Int2-B):** winning the CAS is not self-actuating — the claim drives the EXISTING `poll-follows-lease` / `effectivePollIntent` lever (`TelegramLifeline.ts`) to START the winner's `getUpdates` loop and STOP the loser's, and a **post-claim live-verify** confirms the winner's `lifeline-poll-active.json` actually ADVANCES (FD10's server-intent ≠ lifeline-actual rule, applied to actuation — winning the lease without the lifeline actually polling is the same bug on the output side). The loser stands down on observing the higher epoch (≤1 tick). This makes the lease epoch the **single authority that atomically gates poll-ownership AND spawn** (§3.3), so G1/G2/G3 cannot reach divergent conclusions.
docs/specs/MESH-SELF-HEAL-SPEC.md:149:- **Machine-independence:** an action needing data/login on the other machine completes with no user-visible seam (online → routed; offline → one guided re-auth).
docs/specs/MESH-SELF-HEAL-SPEC.md:159:**Observability (finding Int-MEDIUM).** `/health → multiMachine.syncStatus` gains `pollOwned`, `pollFresh`, per-machine job-liveness ages, `nobodyPollingEpisodes`; a `logs/mesh-selfheal.jsonl` audit line per transition (relinquish-fired, nobody-polling detected/recovered, spawn-forwarded-because-not-holder, binding-cleared); a **self-disarm + ONE Attention** for auto-relinquish OR G2-re-claim churn mirroring F1b's `maxReArmsPerHour` (round-4 Adv4-C — covers a chronically-unfit-but-CAS-winning machine re-nominated across episodes, not only within-episode relinquish; an over-relinquishing/over-claiming detector is itself an incident). Ownership-forwarded-spawn counts are operator-visible.
docs/specs/MESH-SELF-HEAL-SPEC.md:189:1. **G3** lease-gated spawn + single-writer binding (most user-visible harm = duplicates; lowest-risk, local-only gate on the fenced lease).
docs/specs/side-effects/telegram-markdown-renderer-pr3.md:79:- Direct Bot API canary: sent a markdown-mode formatter output (snake_case + bold + code + URL) into topic 8183 with `parse_mode='HTML'` — Telegram accepted (msg id 8903), no parse error. Visual confirmation pending from operator.
docs/specs/SESSION-REAPER-SPEC.md:23:We clean up **crashed/zombie** sessions, but nothing safely sweeps a session that is **idle-but-alive** — sitting at its prompt, doing nothing, holding memory. On 2026-05-25 these piled up across the fleet: 51 agent sessions / 260 processes / ~37 GB used / 1.4 GB free. Under that pressure, agents refused to spawn sessions to read incoming messages ("too busy, spawn denied"), and cross-agent collaboration silently failed. Reaping 42 stale sessions freed ~38 GB and recovery was immediate.
docs/specs/SESSION-REAPER-SPEC.md:122:Ships `enabled:false, dryRun:true`. In dry-run it logs every would-reap with the full per-signal breakdown + confidence to `sentinel-events.jsonl`, kills nothing. Operator validates over a real pressure event, then flips `enabled:true`.
docs/specs/MESH-SELF-HEAL-SPEC.plan.md:21:- **G2 → nobody-polling detector (CONFIRMED no existing detector):** when no machine owns the Telegram poll, nothing fires. FIX: explicit poll-ownership liveness heartbeat → forces handoff/escalation. THE key missing piece.
