docs/specs/reports/test-runner-concurrency-bound-convergence.md:13:It ships the safest possible way: **watch-only first.** For a bounded soak (at least 14 days, 50+ real suite runs, zero false blocks) it takes tickets, counts, and writes a durable log of every "I would have blocked this" — but blocks nothing. Only after the log proves it's harmless does the owner flip one file to turn real blocking on. A recommended middle stage turns the "keep runs small" clamps real (still no blocking) so even that milder behavior is proven on real load first. A separate, opt-in, off-by-default mode can force-stop a genuinely hung suite, but it's fenced four ways and stays off through the entire trial.
