docs/specs/reports/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors-iteration-log.md:160:INT2-1 MAT [§3.2.4a] Commitment has NO session binding field (topicId/boundTuple/boundBy only, CommitmentTracker.ts:35-75); ReapGuard veto is activeCommitmentForTopic(topicId) — TOPIC-scoped; nothing session-shaped to CAS; per-machine store, in-process single-writer queues; survivor's beacon can't drive a record it doesn't hold; maxActiveBeacons boot-cap on transfers unaddressed. → REDESIGN: the two-guard carve-out is the operative piece (topic-scoped guard means record stays valid for topic); replace phantom session re-bind with explicit disposition of the residual open record on the closing machine (owner-gated suppression at PromiseBeacon.emitUserSend chokepoint + audited ownership annotation), OR specify real cross-machine custody incl. beacon-cap. (final shape of the SC2-1/ADV2-2/SEC2-2/DC2-1 cluster)
docs/specs/reports/ownership-gated-spawn-and-judgment-within-floors-iteration-log.md:179:A. Commitment custody (SC2-1+ADV2-2+SEC2-2+DC2-1+INT2-1+LA2-1): kill phantom session re-bind → post-close custody transfer: reconciler reads closing copy's open topic commitments (authed mesh read); OWNER machine mints successor commitments (own API, idempotent externalKey, origin-stamp invariant preserved); origin records → terminal 'superseded-by-ownership-move' (own CAS, audited) ONLY on successor ack; no-ack → escalate; vetoed close → nothing transferred (transfer is post-close); PromiseBeacon owner-other self-suppression covers the gap; sessionEpoch: supersede disarms session-lost; beacon boot-cap: successor respects existing activation cap; posture row; two-node test.
