docs/specs/reports/reviewer-fail-closed-on-abstain-convergence.md:17:The original draft invented a brand-new "critical" reviewer tier. Review caught that the gate code **already has** a `'high'` criticality tier that does exactly the wanted behavior (block external / allow-internal on a high-stakes abstain) — and that nothing in the code reads the value `'critical'`, so the original design would have shipped a **silent no-op**: a safety "fix" that fixed nothing. The converged spec reuses the existing `'high'` mechanism and just routes errored reviewers into it (the real bug: an errored reviewer was mis-counted as a genuine pass, so the existing fail-closed net never fired).
