docs/specs/reports/benchmark-divergence-detector-convergence.md:13:It only ever observes. Every finding is stamped advisory; nothing anywhere may auto-act on one. It ships dark on the fleet and in a write-nothing rehearsal mode on the development agent, and the operator's two requirements are structural: no grade data is deleted before its lesson is captured (the lesson is folded into a permanent summary at grading time), and analysis gathers every machine's data — an offline machine makes the result "partial," never a wrong conclusion.
docs/specs/reports/benchmark-divergence-detector-convergence.md:17:**The retention redesign (round 1, the big one).** The original draft made the quality meter's data-cleanup wait for this detector's progress. Five reviewers independently showed the two default states were both hazardous: detector off (the fleet default) meant the meter's data could never be cleaned up — unbounded growth; rehearsal mode risked marking data "analyzed" while writing nothing. The converged design removes the coupling entirely: per-day, per-model grade tallies live in a new parallel summary table maintained by the meter's own grading machinery, and the detector reads only that. The meter's cleanup is byte-identical whatever the detector does.
docs/specs/reports/benchmark-divergence-detector-convergence.md:21:**Tightening to zero (rounds 3–4).** Round 3 verified every round-2 fix landed genuinely and yielded ten one-line tightenings (examples: fully-ungraded days must still weigh in the honesty gate; a machine-switch must not fabricate months of false "data lost" warnings; peer machines' free-text is dropped and regenerated locally so a compromised machine has no text channel into the reader). Round 4 verified all ten and found nothing new; both external models returned only restatements of trade-offs the spec already documents.
docs/specs/reports/autonomous-completion-discipline-convergence.md:5:When you put the agent in a long, pre-approved autonomous run and walk away, you want it to actually keep going until the work is genuinely done — not quit early because it decided some reversible choice "needs your input," or that finishing a few tasks was a tidy place to pause. We already shipped the *prompt* half of that fix (a "these are the only valid reasons to stop" section in the agent's playbook). This spec is the *structural* half: a stop-gate that actually blocks the session from exiting while real work remains, makes an independent judge (not the agent's own say-so) the arbiter of "is it done," and — when the agent claims it's genuinely blocked by something external it can't fix — requires it to leave a tamper-visible, you-can-acknowledge-it record instead of quietly disappearing.
docs/specs/reports/autonomous-completion-discipline-convergence.md:32:**Iteration 1 (17 material):** (HIGH) prompt-injection into the judge; self-inducible fail-open exit; (CRITICAL, adversarial) the marker was unguarded by P13 + nothing verified the blocker (P13 mis-placed in the draft); (HIGH) marker collides with the `<promise>` whitespace-collapsing extraction + self-trips on its own docs; checkbox scan gameable both ways + sole-signal in promise-fallback; the completion judge framed as O(turns) LLM calls + 10s-vs-35s timeout confusion; (HIGH, integration) config-migration named the wrong mechanism (should be ConfigDefaults), the P13 signal-feed signature/route change omitted, the SKILL.md Step-2b frontmatter template (the load-bearing edit) not flagged; (HIGH, lessons) the objective-signals wiring unimplementable as written, the milestone-phrase class had zero structural floor (pure prompt-willpower), a new manufactured-hard-blocker dishonesty vector, recurrence-risking deferrals (Q3/Q4) + missing `lessons-engaged:`; (MED/LOW) artifact tamper-claim over-stated + unbounded/unsanitized fields (log-injection) + leak surface, denial-of-exit + no scoped operator unblock, marker anti-collision nonce, no-baseline conservatism, in-flight backward-compat, off-switch half-gated, unbounded-run no-backstop, version-skew window, §3.1 over-claim (judge sees prose, can't run tests). — ALL resolved in the iteration-2 spec.
docs/specs/reports/autonomous-completion-discipline-convergence.md:40:**Iteration 5 (0):** adversarial — CONVERGED, no material issues (timeout math/prose correct; revert broke nothing; self-induced-fail-open still handled + disentangled; all prior-closed items unaffected). lessons-aware — CONVERGED, the revert is a Structure>Willpower / verify-before-claiming win with no regression.
