docs/eli16/threadline-honest-delivery-receipts.eli16.md:7:Threadline used one success-shaped result for several very different events: a relay accepted bytes, a receiver queued work, a live session received the message, or a spawn was refused. The final sender-facing tool then turned almost every successful HTTP request into `delivered: true`, so a message that never reached a live agent could look fully delivered.

